                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s HbA1c is elevated, indicating suboptimal long-term glycemic control and suggesting poorly controlled or undiagnosed diabetes mellitus. This increases the risk for microvascular and macrovascular complications, especially at advanced age. Clinical correlation and consideration of antidiabetic therapy adjustment are recommended.</td>
